※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4549

※ A lambda keeps what it brought in, and what it brought in lives in the call
※ that wrote it -- so handing one back would hand back a way of reading storage
※ that is gone.  It is the rule a reference follows, at the same place and for
※ the same reason, and lifetime annotations are what will lift both.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6

fn made() → fn(u8) → u8:
    λ a: u8 → u8 { a }
